ash-walker-recipe-book-fishing =
    { "[" }bold]Fishing in lava[/bold]
    Bone fishing rod: 3 bones, 2 watcher sinews and 1 goliath hide. It comes with a bone hook and heat-resistant line.
    Apply ordinary food to the rod: meat, fish, mushrooms, fruit or a prepared dish. Each use takes a small portion; one food item can supply several portions. The rod holds five portions and each cast consumes one. Open sealed packaging first.
    Hold the rod and cast into lava up to four tiles away, from the shore or a stationary boat. When a fish bites, press the use-item-in-hand key (Z by default) within three seconds.
    Drag the fishing window by its title bar to move it, or drag its edges to resize it. Hold that key to move the colored frame right; release it to move the frame left. Keep the white catch marker inside the frame to fill the catch bar. Progress falls outside the frame. Fill the bar before the catch escapes. Closing the window or pressing "Reel in the line" ends fishing.
    Fish change direction and resist more strongly than objects. A successful fight immediately awards the catch. If your hands are full, it stays on the rod; free a hand and activate the rod to collect it.
    Catches include eels, armored fish, rare pale fish, materials, tools, medicine, toys and junk, with an occasional valuable find. A whole pale fish replaces one carcass in a rite of Return. Cook ordinary fish over the hearth.
    Each area's stocks are limited and gradually recover. Move elsewhere when the area grows quiet. Moving, switching active hands or losing the rod ends the attempt. Use the rod's reel-in action to stop yourself. A failed attempt spends the bait but keeps the rod.
